WEBVTT

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.940
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.820
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.660
but also in crime.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.780
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.490
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.260
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:49.940
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:55.320
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:02.080
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:08.420
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:13.260
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:20.260
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.520
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.520
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:33.610
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:36.610
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:42.830
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:49.130
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.460
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.390
Vocational Options

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.190
Prepare to land.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.610
<i>Within seconds,</i>
<i>the Helldivers are at their target...</i>

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.070
<i>using rapid-fire guns on bunker 3.</i>

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.070
<i>Ready.</i>

00:02:59.240 --> 00:02:59.900
<i>Fire.</i>

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.720
Wow! Pretty impressive, up close.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.100
They only give this demo once a year.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.430
I can see why it's so popular.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.730
Captain! Isn't there some way
we can take one of those guns?

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.020
I suspect they're keeping
a close eye on them.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:40.860
Are you Special Vehicles,
Second Section?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.110
Yes.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.990
I'm Lt. Komiya of the air-drop team.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:51.790
Captain Fuwa asked me
to show you around.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.630
This is so damn cool!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.170
...and as you can see...

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.090
I want one!

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.140
...it's been set from the middle.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.930
Oh, I see!

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:11.680
Thank you for the invitations.
Captain Nagumo sends her best.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.150
Did you like what you saw?

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.110
An excellent demonstration.
We couldn't do half so well.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:23.530
I'd like to ask you something
that's been bothering me.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:29.030
Purely on specs, some of
the new Labors beat our Helldivers.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:33.540
Are these new models
going to be trouble for us?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.040
We're concerned, too,

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.710
but our hectic schedule doesn't
leave much spare time for worry.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:42.920
Of course.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.180
Well, enjoy yourselves.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.600
Captain Fuwa,
the downloads have all finished.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:00.400
Hey, Asuma, who's better?
A Helldiver, or Alphonse?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.530
Helldivers use an Ingram chassis,

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.320
but the missions are so different...

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.950
Yeah, they can't compare.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:09.870
Can you start one up?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.790
Of course.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:12.580
Do it.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:17.290
Officer Izumi, nice to see you again.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.960
Nice to see you again.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:22.250
Interested in the Helldiver?

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.220
He's pretty interesting looking.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.970
Care to try it out?

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.930
I'd like to hear how
it compares to an Ingram.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:38.730
The handling's pretty tricky,
so you may tire quickly.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:42.020
Just let me at him!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.780
Try not to damage it!

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.110
I know.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.040
Okay.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:43.420
Well?

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:45.880
The handling was much easier
than I expected.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:48.590
How did it feel?

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:53.100
Not as smooth as Alphonse,
but he was pretty good.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.100
He had a very light touch.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:59.230
So you give it a passing grade?
Want to ride one permanently?

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.900
We're looking for top pilots.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.610
But I'm happily employed
as a police officer.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.160
True. For now.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:21.620
Enough for today. Dismissed.
Don't be late tomorrow.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:26.920
Officer Izumi!

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.340
Captain Fuwa asked me
to give this to you.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:37.560
What is it?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.100
Reference material.
You may find it useful.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:45.060
Huh? Reference?

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:47.940
Hurry up!

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.820
Wait for me!

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.160
I wonder what it is?

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.580
Open it and find out.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:05.170
But what if it self-destructs in five seconds?

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:09.670
Shinohara AV-99
Operations Manual

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:10.880
It's the manual!

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.590
Why would she give you that?

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.470
She said she was
looking for good pilots.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:19.060
Was she serious
about that job offer?

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:19.720
<i>What</i>?

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:28.940
That's pretty flattering.
And the Helldiver is kind of cute.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:30.650
I better think it over.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:31.280
Are you serious?

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:33.950
Are you really serious?

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:36.660
Of course not.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.700
Besides, I'm sure
she was just joking.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.840
It was incredibly dull here.
Nothing happened.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.720
Well, beware of Greeks bearing gifts.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.220
You're in a sour mood today.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.220
I'm just the suspicious type.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.180
So how did it go yesterday?

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.390
Oh, great. Thanks so much.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:04.890
What's wrong?

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.150
The Self Defense Force
is a breed apart.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:09.400
Well, of course.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.360
Special Vehicles,
Second Section.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.320
Oh, hello.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:22.330
I want you to know I was serious.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.540
<i>Uh, well...</i>

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.000
You'd have the latest equipment,
and plenty of training.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:32.380
Don't you want to improve,
to make a difference?

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.010
We can give you that opportunity.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:38.090
Of course I want to improve,
but this is different...

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:38.470
<i>Different</i>?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.640
<i>I'm really flattered, but...</i>

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.140
Target practice is beginning.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.230
I'll be right there.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.900
Let's get together soon.
Okay, bye.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.110
Lt. Komiya, why did you apply
for the air-drop team?

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:03.080
Ever since childhood,
I have dreamed of being a Labor pilot.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:07.040
Good enough for me.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.300
<i>There is a 402 on the Kawasaki side,</i>
<i>at the breakwater.</i>

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.220
<i>Division 2, prepare to mobilize.</i>
<i>I repeat...</i>

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:31.440
Noa!

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.070
What?

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.070
Did Fuwa just call you?

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:37.820
What'd she say?

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.150
Well, uh...

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:43.330
Get moving, you two!
We have to mobilize!

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:45.410
Later.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:08.770
We'll lift the crane so you can
move the steel frame.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.770
Be careful, the pilot's inside.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.020
Roger!

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.490
<i>Try to prevent</i>
<i>any vibrations or shocks.</i>

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.330
<i>We don't want another collapse.</i>

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.120
Roger.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.000
<i>More carefully, Officer Ota.</i>

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.210
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.530
<i>Check on the pilot.</i>

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.250
<i>Noa, what are you doing</i>?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:12.910
Huh? Oh, roger.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.140
I... I...

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.140
<i>Noa, what are you doing</i>?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.060
<i>This is no time for daydreaming!</i>
<i>Help Ota!</i>

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:02.010
I expect better from you.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.300
I'm very sorry. I was distracted.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:11.010
Our work doesn't give time-outs
or second chances.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.730
When we mobilize, it's for real.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:18.190
Try to keep focused from now on.
That's all.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.520
Yes, sir. Thank you very much.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.990
Is the pilot going to be okay?

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:31.200
He's conscious,
so I think he'll be okay.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:35.660
What point does my job have,
if I can't save people?

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:39.380
That's why we have practice.
Learn something from this.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.420
Well, let's go. Everyone's waiting.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:52.510
Okay, get with it!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:15.830
Miss Izumi looks really depressed.
Is she okay?

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.000
She'll snap out of it soon.
She's pretty simple.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.760
Machine 2, you're out of bullets.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.050
Fast practices are so unsatisfying!

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.770
Paint bullets are expensive.

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.100
<i>We aren't the Self Defense Force!</i>

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.230
<i>That's all, Miss Izumi.</i>

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.660
Catching criminals
requires marksmanship!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.290
We need to have more practice!

00:14:56.490 --> 00:15:00.210
But we do more than that!
We handle accidents and disasters.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.290
We can't spend all our time
on target practice.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:05.550
Exactly. Balance is essential.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:10.260
We must conquer weaknesses
while polishing strengths. Understand?

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:11.470
Yes!

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:13.010
Good.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:22.940
Are you still at it?

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.320
He's covered in gunpowder.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.440
See you later.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.280
Asuma...

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:32.450
Why do you do this?

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:33.700
How about you?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:34.950
You first.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.410
I'll tell you after you tell me.

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:39.620
I'm too embarrassed.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.580
Yeah, right.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.920
Take care. Bye.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.510
Just a little more polishing.

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:00.240
Hello.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:03.660
Are you thirsty?

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.130
Were you watching
that whole thing?

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.300
Let's go talk.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.930
Thanks for the loan.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:27.850
Hold on to it.
After all, I have the original.

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:29.270
It's just that...

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:31.980
Did you think I was joking?

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.990
No, but I like my current line of work.

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:41.280
Don't worry. Most of what we do
is the same as Special Vehicles.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.460
I know you don't hate Labors.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:47.750
I like them.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:51.130
Then why don't you want
to improve your skills?

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.670
I do.
But that isn't the real question.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:54.960
What is?

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:11.770
Help!

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:17.740
I've been robbed!
He's in that car! Police!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.200
Call it in for me!

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:25.580
Miss Izumi!

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:41.720
I can use the back roads
to cut ahead of him.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:55.020
Excuse me!

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:56.900
You idiot!

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:17.090
Get out of your car!
You're under arrest for robbery!

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.810
Running only makes it worse!

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:35.690
You won't get away!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.340
Officer Izumi, get in.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.550
Now we've got him.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.770
Pull over and halt.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:15.230
Stop your car.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.820
Didn't you hear me?
Stop your car!

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.180
Halt.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.110
Just try and get me!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.280
Try it!

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:12.910
Never underestimate
a policewoman!

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:36.060
I'm glad no one was hurt.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:38.150
But somebody was.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:39.810
Your left cheek.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:44.440
Oh, this? It's nothing.

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:48.410
I'll take my manual back now.

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:51.830
I'm giving up.

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:09.390
Good morning!

00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:10.720
Morning. You're early.

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:17.310
Good morning.

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:18.440
Morning.

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:20.230
I gave back the manual.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:21.060
Oh.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:26.650
What? Did something happen
yesterday? Did you see Fuwa?

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:31.700
It's too embarrassing.

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:38.410
You have to tell me!
Please? Pretty please?

00:23:01.100 --> 00:23:06.400
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:14.160
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:16.040
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:21.580
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:29.550
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:31.260
I got it

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:38.810
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:44.690
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:46.230
One more chance

00:23:46.230 --> 00:23:53.870
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:53.870 --> 00:23:59.790
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:03.880
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:13.220
This story is fiction...

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:13.220
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:21.930
In a hurry, Division 1 gets assigned
a new Labor: AV Zero.

00:24:21.930 --> 00:24:25.350
But Special Vehicles as a rule usually tries
to avoid unnecessary conflict.

00:24:25.810 --> 00:24:27.610
Where's that bravery of
the Self Defense Forces.

00:24:27.610 --> 00:24:32.610
Seems like the Ingram is getting
ridiculed. What will you do, Noa?

00:24:32.610 --> 00:24:34.820
Alphonse will not lose to Zero!

00:24:35.490 --> 00:24:39.120
Next Episode: His Name is Zero.
Target, locked on!

00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:44.120
Next episode

00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:44.120
His Name is Zero
